# Booking confirmation reminders (email) — backend reference

This document describes the backend implementation for the **Booking confirmation Reminders** settings UI (email only; WhatsApp is intentionally not implemented here).

Related Markdown guides: `docs/BOOKING_CONFIRMATION_REMINDERS_API.md` (curl examples and QA checklist), `docs/BOOKING_CONFIRMATION_REMINDERS_E2E_TESTING.md` (dispatch + related endpoints, full request/response examples).

---

## 1. Purpose

- Persist the master **Reminder** toggle, per-business **schedules** (hours/days before appointment, optional time-of-day for day-based rules), and the **email subject + body** template.
- Evaluate **work orders** with a concrete `scheduledAt`, send at most **one email per schedule row per work order**, and honour the UI rule about **missed reminder windows**.
- Expose **template variable metadata** for the **Insert variable** dropdown (same token style as `GET /api/clients/{clientId}/message-template`).

---

## 2. Persistence (Prisma)

| UI / concept | Storage |
| --- | --- |
| Reminder ON/OFF | `BusinessSettings.bookingRemindersEnabled` |
| Each schedule row | `ReminderConfig` with `reminderType = BOOKING_CONFIRMATION`, `channel = EMAIL`, `timeValue`, `timeUnit` (`hours` \| `days`), `timeOfDay` (nullable; used for `days`), `isEnabled` |
| Email subject + message | `MessageTemplate` with `templateType = BOOKING_CONFIRMATION_REMINDER`, `channel = EMAIL`, linked to `BusinessSettings` |
| Sent audit / dedupe | `ReminderLog` with `reminderType = BOOKING_CONFIRMATION`, `entityType = WORK_ORDER`, `workOrderId`, `clientId`, `businessId`, `channel = EMAIL`, `note = configId:<ReminderConfig.id>` |

Business timezone for day-based wall times: `Business.timeZone` (IANA), e.g. `America/Santiago`. When the JS runtime exposes `Temporal`, day offsets + `timeOfDay` use that timezone; otherwise a UTC fallback is used (see service comments in code).

---

## 3. HTTP API (authenticated)

Base path: `/api/settings` (same router as other company settings).

| Method | Path | Permission | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/booking-confirmation-reminders` | `settings` `read` | Toggle, schedules, template, `uiHint` (exact UI disclaimer text). |
| PATCH | `/booking-confirmation-reminders` | `settings` `update` | Replace all `BOOKING_CONFIRMATION` EMAIL `ReminderConfig` rows for the business and upsert the reminder `MessageTemplate`; update `bookingRemindersEnabled`. |
| POST | `/booking-confirmation-reminders/dispatch` | `settings` `update` | Run dispatch for **this business only** (optional JSON `{ "asOf"?: ISO8601, "dryRun"?: boolean }`, default `{}` → now, `dryRun: false`). |
| GET | `/booking-confirmation-reminders/template-variables` | `settings` `read` | Static list of `{ key, label, example }` plus `insertFormat` and `note` for editors. |

Response envelope matches the rest of the API: `{ message, success, data }`.

---

## 4. Master toggle behaviour

- **Default ON:** New `BusinessSettings` rows use `bookingRemindersEnabled` **true** (Prisma `@default(true)` and explicit create in `business.service.ts` when seeding reply-to). The GET settings API also treats a missing row as **enabled** (`?? true`) until persisted otherwise.
- **Automatic emails:** When the toggle is **true**, the server **does not require** POST `/dispatch`. It runs `triggerBookingConfirmationRemindersForAllBusinesses()` on startup and **every ~60 seconds** (`src/index.ts`), same interval as client follow-up reminders. Each run evaluates all businesses and sends **due** reminder emails (same rules as manual dispatch).
- If `bookingRemindersEnabled` is **false**, dispatch exits immediately with `skippedReasons.bookingReminderDisabled` and **sends no email**; the periodic job hits the same fast path.

---

## 5. Dispatch rules (email)

Evaluation starts from **work orders only**. A client who has **never had a work order** (or only quotes/invoices with no job) **never receives** a booking confirmation reminder from this flow — emails are only triggered per qualifying `WorkOrder`.

Work orders considered:

- `businessId` matches.
- `cancelledAt` is null.
- `scheduledAt` is not null.
- **`workOrderNumber` is non-null** (legacy rows missing a number are skipped; counters: `skippedReasons.noWorkOrderNumber`).

**Work-order suppression (before schedule evaluation):**

- **`WorkOrder.bookingConfirmationSentAt`** — set when **Send booking confirmation** runs from Communications / work order (`POST /api/workorders/{id}/send-booking-confirmation`). That job is skipped for automation (`skippedReasons.suppressedAfterBookingConfirmationEmail`).
- **`WorkOrder.confirmationReminderSentAt`** — set when a **manual customer reminder** is created from Clients (`POST /api/clients/{id}/customer-reminders`) or from a work order (`POST /api/workorders/{id}/customer-reminders`). All enabled schedule rows are skipped for that work order (`skippedReasons.suppressedByManualCustomerReminder`). Client-level create stamps **non-cancelled** work orders whose **`scheduledAt` is strictly after “now”** (upcoming appointments only).

For each **enabled** `ReminderConfig` (EMAIL, `BOOKING_CONFIRMATION`) × remaining work order:

1. **Duplicate** — if a `ReminderLog` exists with the same `workOrderId` and `note = configId:<id>`, skip (`alreadySentForSchedule`). This limits **automated** settings reminders to **once** per schedule row per work order after all suppression checks above.
2. **Client email** — if the client has no usable email, skip (`noClientEmail`).
3. **Compute `reminderTime`** from `scheduledAt`, `timeValue`, `timeUnit`, optional `timeOfDay`, and business `timeZone`.
4. **Not due yet** — if `asOf < reminderTime`, skip (`notDueYet`).
5. **Missed scheduling window** — if `reminderTime < workOrder.createdAt`, skip (`missedWindow`). This encodes the UI example: a “6 hours before” rule when the job is only 4 hours away implies a fire time before the work order existed, so no email is sent.
6. **Appointment already started** — if `asOf >= scheduledAt`, skip (`missedWindow`).
7. Otherwise **send** (unless `dryRun`): merge template with variables from the work order context, send via `emailService`, then insert `ReminderLog`.

`skipped` in the dispatch payload is the **sum** of all `skippedReasons` counters. `sent` counts emails that were sent (or that **would** be sent when `dryRun: true`).

---

## 6. Template variables (Insert variable)

Tokens use **single braces**: `{client_name}`, `{job_date}`, etc., and optional legacy **`{{CLIENT_NAME}}`**-style tokens are also substituted in the service.

`GET /api/settings/booking-confirmation-reminders/template-variables` returns the canonical list. Values at send time are built from the **work order** (client, business, WO fields, latest related quote/invoice line items where applicable), aligned with the variable map returned on `GET /api/clients/{clientId}/message-template` for editor consistency.

Extra alias: `{business_name}` maps to the same value as `{company_name}`.

---

## 7. Default template

If no `MessageTemplate` row exists yet, the API reads logical defaults matching the product copy:

- Subject: `Scheduled reminder: Booking confirmation Reminders`
- Message: short greeting with `{client_name}` and reminder text (see `DEFAULT_MESSAGE` in `booking-confirmation-reminders.service.ts`).

---

## 8. Operational notes

- **Resend** — requires `RESEND_API_KEY` and `RESEND_FROM_EMAIL` (or defaults used elsewhere in the codebase) or dispatch will error on send.
- **Dry run** — does not write `ReminderLog` or call Resend; increments `sent` only for rows that would qualify, for observability.
- **PATCH schedules array** — may be empty: all booking email reminder configs are removed; the toggle can still be updated.

---

## 9. Source files

- `src/services/booking-confirmation-reminders.service.ts` — core logic.
- `src/routes/settings/settings.routes.ts` — OpenAPI route definitions.
- `src/routes/settings/settings.handler.ts` — HTTP handlers.
- `src/index.ts` — periodic `triggerBookingConfirmationRemindersForAllBusinesses`.
